<% page_title "Landing carousel" %>

<div id="c-admin-landing-settings">
  <div id="a-show">
    <h1>Landing carousel</h1>

    <h2>The whole carousel</h2>
    <p class="hint">
      How fast every row moves. What each row shows -- the "new" row's board
      included -- is set on the row itself, under Categories.
    </p>

    <%# ONE CONTROL PER SETTING. This form also offered the "new" row's heading,
        board and fresh-only toggle, on LandingSetting -- which nothing has read
        since the rows moved onto LandingCategory (2026-09-17, 8b8f06cee).
        Saving them flashed "The front page now shows ..." and changed nothing,
        beside the Categories form below that edits the row the showcase
        actually reads. Two controls for one setting, one of them dead and
        saying otherwise, so the dead one went. %>
    <%= edit_form_for(@landing_setting, url: admin_landing_setting_path, method: :patch) do |f| %>
      <%= f.input :advance_ms, label: "Slide speed (ms)",
                  hint: "How long a slide holds before the next one. #{LandingSetting::ADVANCE_MS_RANGE.min} to " \
                        "#{LandingSetting::ADVANCE_MS_RANGE.max}; 6000 is six seconds. Below about a second a slide " \
                        "cannot be read before it leaves, and the carousel becomes a permanent animation on the page " \
                        "the bare domain serves to everyone." %>
      <%= f.submit "Save" %>
    <% end %>

    <h2>Categories</h2>
    <p class="hint">
      The rows the carousel switches between, in order. A row with nothing to
      show is dropped rather than rendered blank, so turning one off and
      emptying one look the same to a visitor and only one of them is on
      purpose.
    </p>
    <p class="hint">
      Each row is a set of choices rather than a box you type a search into,
      and each shows the searches it will run. Two terms is the limit: a
      logged-out visitor may search two tags and the landing page runs as
      whoever is looking at it, so a third term would not narrow a row, it
      would empty it -- and an empty row is dropped from the page silently.
    </p>

    <%= form_with url: categories_admin_landing_setting_path, method: :patch, class: "landing-categories" do %>
      <% @landing_categories.each do |category| %>
        <% name = ->(attr) { "landing_categories[#{category.key}][#{attr}]" } %>
        <fieldset class="landing-category" data-kind="<%= category.kind %>" data-key="<%= category.key %>">
          <legend><%= category.label %> <span class="hint">(<%= category.kind %>)</span></legend>

          <div class="input">
            <%= hidden_field_tag name.call(:enabled), "0", id: nil %>
            <%= check_box_tag name.call(:enabled), "1", category.enabled?, id: "landing-#{category.key}-enabled" %>
            <%= label_tag "landing-#{category.key}-enabled", "Show this row" %>
          </div>

          <div class="input">
            <%= label_tag "landing-#{category.key}-label", "Heading" %>
            <%= text_field_tag name.call(:label), category.label, id: "landing-#{category.key}-label", maxlength: 40 %>
          </div>

          <% if category.kind == "board" %>
            <div class="input">
              <%= label_tag "landing-#{category.key}-board", "Board" %>
              <%= text_field_tag name.call(:board), category.board, id: "landing-#{category.key}-board", size: 6 %>
              <span class="hint">The bare slug, so 'b' for /b/.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="input">
              <%= hidden_field_tag name.call(:fresh_only), "0", id: nil %>
              <%= check_box_tag name.call(:fresh_only), "1", category.fresh_only?, id: "landing-#{category.key}-fresh" %>
              <%= label_tag "landing-#{category.key}-fresh", "Freshly scraped only" %>
            </div>
          <% elsif category.kind == "tags" %>
            <%# THE CREATORS AS THEMSELVES: each listed tag is drawn as its pill --
                an artist as the site's artist pill with its activity lamp, lit
                while they have posted inside the creator window -- with a remove
                control beside it, and an input that adds one, picked from the
                site's tag completer. The hidden field is what the form sends,
                the same space-separated list the text box sent, so nothing
                server-side changed. A tag that does not exist is named in a
                warning, because it does not error -- it finds nothing, and the
                row silently loses that creator. %>
            <% categories_by_name = Tag.where(name: category.tags).pluck(:name, :category).to_h.transform_values { |c| TagCategory.reverse_mapping[c] } %>
            <% live = CreatorActivity.active(category.tags.select { |t| categories_by_name[t] == "artist" }) %>
            <% missing = category.tags.reject { |t| categories_by_name.key?(t) } %>
            <div class="input landing-creators" data-landing-creators
                 data-live="<%= live.to_json %>" data-window="<%= Danbooru.config.creator_active_window.to_i %>">
              <%= label_tag "landing-#{category.key}-add", category.key == "featured" ? "Creators" : "Tags" %>
              <%= hidden_field_tag name.call(:tags_string), category.tags_string, id: "landing-#{category.key}-tags", data: { creators_value: true } %>
              <span class="landing-creator-pills" data-creators-list>
                <% category.tags.each do |tag_name| %>
                  <% kind = categories_by_name[tag_name] %>
                  <span class="landing-creator" data-name="<%= tag_name %>">
                    <% if kind.nil? %>
                      <span class="mod-pill mod-pill--pending" title="No tag by this name exists, so this search finds nothing"><%= tag_name.tr("_", " ") %></span>
                    <% elsif kind.in?(%w[artist copyright character]) %>
                      <%= link_to posts_path(tags: tag_name), class: "mod-pill mod-pill--cat mod-pill--cat-#{kind}#{" is-live" if live.include?(tag_name)}",
                                  data: { tag: tag_name }, target: "_blank" do %>
                        <% if kind == "artist" %><span class="mod-pill-dot"></span><% end %>
                        <%= tag_name.tr("_", " ") %>
                      <% end %>
                    <% else %>
                      <%= link_to tag_name.tr("_", " "), posts_path(tags: tag_name), class: "mod-pill mod-pill--meta", title: "a #{kind} tag, not a creator", target: "_blank" %>
                    <% end %>
                    <button type="button" class="landing-creator-x" data-act="creator-remove" title="remove <%= tag_name %>" aria-label="remove <%= tag_name %>">&times;</button>
                  </span>
                <% end %>
              </span>
              <% if missing.any? %>
                <p class="hint landing-creators-missing">
                  <strong>No such tag:</strong> <%= missing.join(", ") %> -- these find nothing. Remove them, or correct the spelling.
                </p>
              <% end %>
              <%= text_field_tag nil, nil, id: "landing-#{category.key}-add", class: "landing-creator-add",
                                 placeholder: "add #{category.key == "featured" ? "a creator" : "a tag"}, then Enter",
                                 autocomplete: "off", data: { autocomplete: "tag", creators_add: true } %>
              <span class="hint">
                <strong><span data-tag-count="landing-<%= category.key %>-tags"><%= category.tags.length %></span>
                of <%= LandingCategory::MAX_TAGS %></strong> listed; an added one is saved with "Save carousel".
                <strong>Each tag is searched on its own</strong>, not all together:
                twenty creators is twenty one-term searches, run in the background
                and cached, because an anonymous visitor may search only
                <%= LandingCategory::MAX_TERMS %> tags and this page runs as
                whoever is looking at it. Leave empty to show everything in the
                chosen order.
              </span>
            </div>
          <% elsif category.kind == "galleries" %>
            <p class="hint">
              This row shows the galleries of PROMOTED creators, newest promotion
              first, one slide each before anyone gets a second. It is set by
              promoting a gallery, not from here -- the flag is
              <code>promoted_at</code> on the gallery.
            </p>
          <% elsif category.kind == "blog" %>
            <p class="hint">
              This row shows the blog's newest posts -- title, author, blurb and
              picture, each card linking to the post on the blog. It reads the
              blog's own index, <code><%= LandingBlogCache.index_url %></code>, in
              the background every <%= LandingBlogCache::STALE_AFTER.inspect %>:
              to put a post here, publish it on the blog. A different index is
              <code>landing_blog_index_url</code> in the booru's config.
            </p>
            <%# THE LAST READ, in one of four states, because an unread or failing
                index looks exactly like an empty blog from the front page -- the
                row is simply absent. Read from LandingBlogCache, which records
                every attempt; never rendered as healthy unless a recent read was. %>
            <% blog_status = LandingBlogCache.status %>
            <% blog_posts = LandingBlogCache.posts %>
            <% if blog_status.nil? %>
              <p class="hint" data-blog-status="never">
                <strong>Not read yet.</strong> The first visit to the front page,
                or the next scheduled refresh, reads it. If this stays, the
                background worker (the jobs and cron containers) is not running.
              </p>
            <% elsif !blog_status[:ok] %>
              <p class="hint" data-blog-status="failed">
                <strong>The last read failed</strong>, <%= time_ago_in_words(Time.zone.at(blog_status[:at])) %> ago:
                <%= blog_status[:error] %>.
                <% if blog_posts.any? %>
                  The row is still showing <%= pluralize(blog_posts.size, "post") %> from the last read that
                  worked, for up to <%= LandingBlogCache::TTL.inspect %> after it.
                <% else %>
                  Nothing is left to show, so the row is off the front page until a read succeeds.
                <% end %>
              </p>
            <% elsif Time.zone.now.to_i - blog_status[:at] > 2 * LandingBlogCache::STALE_AFTER.to_i %>
              <p class="hint" data-blog-status="stalled">
                <strong>Last read <%= time_ago_in_words(Time.zone.at(blog_status[:at])) %> ago</strong>,
                though it is read every <%= LandingBlogCache::STALE_AFTER.inspect %>: nothing has tried
                since, so the background worker (the jobs and cron containers) may be down.
                That read found <%= pluralize(blog_status[:count], "post") %>.
              </p>
            <% else %>
              <p class="hint" data-blog-status="ok">
                <strong>Read <%= time_ago_in_words(Time.zone.at(blog_status[:at])) %> ago:</strong>
                <%= pluralize(blog_status[:count], "post") %> of the <%= blog_status[:listed] %> the index lists
                (<%= blog_posts.count { it[:image] } %> with a picture, <%= blog_posts.count { it[:author] } %> naming an author).
                <% if blog_status[:count].zero? %>
                  With nothing to show, the row is off the front page.
                <% end %>
              </p>
            <% end %>
            <% if blog_status.present? && blog_status[:problems].present? %>
              <ul class="hint list-bulleted" data-blog-problems>
                <% blog_status[:problems].each do |problem| %>
                  <li><%= problem %></li>
                <% end %>
              </ul>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>

          <% if category.kind.in?(%w[tags blog]) %>
            <div class="input">
              <%= label_tag "landing-#{category.key}-slides", "Slides on screen" %>
              <%= number_field_tag name.call(:slides), category.slides,
                                   id: "landing-#{category.key}-slides", size: 4,
                                   min: LandingCategory::SLIDES_RANGE.min, max: LandingCategory::SLIDES_RANGE.max,
                                   placeholder: "belt default" %>
              <span class="hint">
                How many slides this row shows at once. <strong>Presentation
                only</strong> -- it does not change which posts the row holds
                or how far it advances before repeating. That is
                <%= category.kind == "blog" ? "the blog itself" : "the creator list and the order, below" %>.
                Leave it empty for the belt's own default.
                <%= LandingCategory::SLIDES_RANGE.min %> to <%= LandingCategory::SLIDES_RANGE.max %>.
                The belt is symmetric about the focused slide, so an even number
                rounds up to the next odd one rather than hiding a slide. The
                belt is as wide as the page: on a wide run the outer slides
                shrink and thin toward the edges, and what does not fit is off
                screen until the run advances.
              </span>
            </div>
          <% end %>

          <% if category.kind.in?(%w[board tags]) %>
            <div class="input">
              <%= label_tag "landing-#{category.key}-ordering", "Order" %>
              <%= select_tag name.call(:ordering),
                             options_for_select(LandingCategory::ORDERINGS.keys, category.ordering),
                             id: "landing-#{category.key}-ordering" %>
              <span class="hint">
                "new" spends no term and keeps the row behaving as a queue: a new
                post enters at the front and the last falls off the back, so
                nothing shuffles on its own. "random" reshuffles the row every
                time its candidates are refreshed -- see below for when that is.
                Order applies to tag rows; a board row's search is already two
                terms and carries no order term.
              </span>
            </div>
          <% end %>

          <% unless category.kind == "blog" %>
          <p class="hint">
            <%# safe_join with a tag per query, NOT a joined string marked html_safe.
                The queries are assembled from a validated board slug and validated
                tag names, so nothing dangerous can reach here today -- and that is
                an argument about the validators, not about this line. Escaping each
                one keeps it true if a validator is ever loosened. %>
            Searches:
            <% if category.queries.any? %>
              <%= safe_join(category.queries.map { |q| tag.code(q) }, " ") %>
            <% else %>
              (none)
            <% end %>
          </p>
          <% end %>
        </fieldset>
      <% end %>

      <%= submit_tag "Save carousel" %>
    <% end %>

    <%# THE CREATOR EDITOR (see the tags row above). Removing a pill or adding
        a name rewrites the hidden field the form sends and the "N of 50"
        count, so the admin sees the count before saving rather than an error
        after. A name added here is drawn as an UNSAVED pill: its category and
        lamp are the server's to say, on the next render after Save. The lamps
        of the saved pills are re-read while the page is open (creator_lamps.js).
        The slides placeholder no longer follows the count: slides on screen is
        a presentation value and is not derived from the creator list
        (operator ruling 2026-09-22), so its default is the belt's own. %>
    <script>
      document.querySelectorAll("[data-landing-creators]").forEach(function (box) {
        var value = box.querySelector("[data-creators-value]");
        var list = box.querySelector("[data-creators-list]");
        var add = box.querySelector("[data-creators-add]");
        var count = document.querySelector('[data-tag-count="' + value.id + '"]');
        var names = function () {
          return Array.from(list.querySelectorAll(".landing-creator")).map(function (el) { return el.dataset.name; });
        };
        var sync = function () {
          var all = names();
          value.value = all.join(" ");
          if (count) count.textContent = String(all.length);
        };
        var addName = function (raw) {
          var name = String(raw || "").trim().toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, "_");
          add.value = "";
          if (!name || names().indexOf(name) !== -1) return;
          var row = document.createElement("span");
          row.className = "landing-creator";
          row.dataset.name = name;
          var pill = document.createElement("span");
          pill.className = "mod-pill mod-pill--pending";
          pill.title = "Added -- saved when you press Save carousel";
          pill.textContent = name.replace(/_/g, " ");
          var x = document.createElement("button");
          x.type = "button";
          x.className = "landing-creator-x";
          x.dataset.act = "creator-remove";
          x.setAttribute("aria-label", "remove " + name);
          x.innerHTML = "&times;";
          row.append(pill, x);
          list.appendChild(row);
          sync();
        };
        list.addEventListener("click", function (e) {
          var x = e.target.closest("[data-act='creator-remove']");
          if (!x) return;
          x.closest(".landing-creator").remove();
          sync();
        });
        // Enter adds what is typed and never submits the whole form -- unless
        // the completer's menu is choosing, in which case its pick is added.
        add.addEventListener("keydown", function (e) {
          if (e.key !== "Enter") return;
          e.preventDefault();
          var ac = window.jQuery && window.jQuery(add).data("ui-autocomplete");
          if (ac && ac.menu && ac.menu.active) return;
          addName(add.value);
        });
        if (window.jQuery) {
          window.jQuery(add).on("autocompleteselect", function (e, ui) {
            addName(ui.item.value);
            setTimeout(function () { add.value = ""; }, 0);
          });
        }
        if (window.Danbooru && window.Danbooru.CreatorLamps) {
          new window.Danbooru.CreatorLamps(box, {
            live: JSON.parse(box.dataset.live || "[]"),
            windowSeconds: Number(box.dataset.window) || 300,
          }).start();
        }
      });
    </script>

    <h2>When the searches run</h2>
    <p class="hint">
      Two different clocks, because the rows are two different kinds of thing.
      Every number here is read from the code that enforces it.
    </p>
    <ul class="hint list-bulleted">
      <li>
        <strong>A board row</strong> ("<%= @landing_categories.find { |c| c.kind == "board" }&.label || "Fresh from DEGEN" %>")
        is one bounded search, run <strong>on every page load</strong> as whoever is
        looking, with a <%= LandingShowcase::QUERY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS %>-second cap. It is
        live by design: a new capture appears at the front of the row within the minute.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A tag row</strong> with more than one creator is
        <strong>never searched on a page load</strong>. A background job runs one search
        per creator (up to <%= LandingCategory::MAX_TAGS %>, keeping
        <%= LandingShowcaseCache::PER_TAG %> posts each, interleaved so every creator
        gets a slide before anyone gets a second) and stores the post ids. A visit
        reads that list. When a visit finds the list older than
        <strong><%= LandingShowcaseCache::STALE_AFTER.inspect %></strong> it is served
        the old list at once and a refresh is queued behind it -- at most one queue
        per row per <%= LandingShowcaseCache::ENQUEUE_DEBOUNCE.inspect %>, however many
        visitors arrive. Independently of visits, a scheduled job refreshes every such
        row <strong>every <%= LandingShowcaseCache::REFRESH_EVERY.inspect %></strong>,
        so a quiet site does not go cold and a busy one is never searched more
        often than that. A stored list is kept for
        <%= LandingShowcaseCache::TTL.inspect %> at most if every refresh fails.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The blog row</strong> runs no search. It reads the blog's index on the
        same clock as the tag rows, as its own job: a visit that finds the read missing
        or older than <%= LandingBlogCache::STALE_AFTER.inspect %> is served what is there
        and queues a read, and the scheduled job reads it every
        <%= LandingShowcaseCache::REFRESH_EVERY.inspect %>. A failed read never replaces
        a good one; the last good read is kept for <%= LandingBlogCache::TTL.inspect %>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Editing a row's tags or order changes its cache key, so the next visit
        sees an empty row once and a fresh search is queued immediately.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>
